Third-party material
--------------------

The Classic Era quest data in Data/Classic/ is derived from the quest database
of Questie (https://github.com/Questie/Questie), which is distributed under the
GNU General Public License version 3.

Modifications made by Ironship, 30 August 2026:

  * Quest titles and objective text were extracted for Classic Era quest ids
    and rewritten into this addon's own Lua table format.
  * Fields this addon does not use -- quest givers, coordinates, level and
    faction requirements, quest chains, reward tables and objective spawn
    data -- were dropped.
  * No quest text was altered. Where the upstream database has no offer text
    for a quest, this addon has none either and says so rather than inventing
    one.

The extraction is performed by Tools/extract_classic_quests.lua, which is part
of the corresponding source of this work.

The English progress and hand-in lines come from the MultiLanguage addon by
Ruben Zantingh (https://github.com/rubenzantingh/MultiLanguage), used with his
permission given on 2 September 2026.

Blizzard's Game Data API publishes a quest's opening text and objectives and
nothing else. It does not publish the line an NPC speaks while a quest is in
progress, nor the one spoken at hand-in, so this panel could only ever show the
opening text at those two moments and print a caveat admitting it was the wrong
passage.

Modifications made by Ironship, 2 September 2026:

  * 17,138 progress lines and 30,780 hand-in lines were taken, together with
    38,390 objective lines and 18,226 quests the API does not return at all.
  * They were rewritten into this addon's own Lua table format. Fields this
    addon does not use were dropped.
  * No quest text was altered. Where a quest still has no progress or hand-in
    line, the panel says so rather than showing the opening text in its place.

The import is performed by Tools/import_multilanguage.py, which is part of the
corresponding source of this work.

